                    insight_cultivated:     `Cultivated learning organisation: you matched communities to tacit/cross-domain knowledge and hierarchy to stable knowledge, resourced and sponsored without over-formalising, held the protected time, and captured the retiring architects — reuse rose on genuine engagement, not paper.`,
                    insight_paper:          `Paper reuse: the headline rate moved, but it rests on a mandated community or a repository nobody owns. This is the 9%-compliance pattern with a better label — it collapses the moment the pressure or the launch energy lifts.`,
                    insight_thin:           `You moved the reuse number but the community is thin. Reuse without genuine engagement is fragile and likely to decay back toward the 9% floor.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the ≥55% reuse target. At the 12-month review the CEO concludes knowledge management 'doesn't work here', disbands the function, and the €11M waste continues. Re-examine which structure you mismatched.`,
                    insight_lowengagement:  `Community engagement stayed low — you launched structures with no fuel. Engagement comes from resourced leaders, protected time and sponsorship without over-formalising, not from mandates.`,
                    insight_lowinnovation:  `Innovation output stayed low — cross-sector idea flow needs tacit knowledge actually moving between units, including the retiring architects' judgment. A repository alone won't produce it.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `You committed more than the €1.2M budget — over-investing in structure engineers won't use repeats the failure of the 9%-compliance portal.`,
                    insight_recovered:      `You recovered a meaningful share of the €11M waste with genuine reuse — a fundable case the CEO will renew, with the retiring expertise protected.`,

                    hint_repository:        `You've leaned into a codified repository — the model that hit 9% compliance. Shift the budget toward communities and socialisation; codification doesn't move tacit, cross-domain knowledge.`,
                    hint_mandate:           `You've mandated the communities into a reporting bureaucracy. Voluntary participation is what makes a community produce knowledge — cultivate with sponsorship and protected time, don't command.`,
                    hint_engagement:        `Community engagement is dangerously low — the structures have no fuel. Resource credible leaders, ring-fence real time, and sponsor without over-formalising.`,
